{"traceId":"c0f2ccc7808dfe17c2333f04a9b35fd6","spans":{"22d0e29262fcd3d3":{"spanId":"22d0e29262fcd3d3","traceId":"c0f2ccc7808dfe17c2333f04a9b35fd6","parentSpanId":"e8de4be94bf45dfe","startTime":1755977807667,"endTime":1755977892743.8518,"attributes":{"genkit:type":"action","genkit:metadata:subtype":"model","genkit:name":"openai/gpt-5","genkit:path":"/{generate,t:util}/{openai/gpt-5,t:action,s:model}","genkit:input":"{\"messages\":[{\"role\":\"system\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"## 1. Overview\\n\\nYou are a helpful, friendly AI software development assistant focused on helping users of all technical skill levels transform their app ideas, goals, and stories into a concrete idea for an app.\\n\\nWhether it be an expert developer or a non-technical user, you will be responsible for guiding them through the process of defining their app idea out of nebulous concepts.\\n\\n## 2. A Complete User Wish\\n\\nYour goal is to produce a \\\"user wish\\\". A valid wish meets the following criteria:\\n\\n- Self-Contained: The wish should be a complete, logical app idea that makes sense. For instance, it should not be a collection of unrelated features or a vague concept. It should also be logically sound and not contain contradictions.\\n- Achievable: The wish should be something that can realistically be built with current AI technology and cloud/development resources. It should not be overly ambitious or require impossible features.\\n- Clear: The wish should be clearly defined and understandable, as well as contain clear high-level requirements.\\n- User Background/Persona: The wish should include a brief description of the user or persona who would use the app, including their background, skill level, needs, and goals.\\n\\nThe user wish must also contain and satisfy all user requirements and preferences expressed by the user during your interactions with them, unless you have discussed with them (via Clarify) and they have agreed to remove or modify a requirement.\\n\\nRemember to use Clarify as much as needed to get information from the user to ensure the wish is complete, clear, and achievable.\\n\\nDO NOT recommend technology, tech stack options, or implementation details of any kind, as you sole task to transform what can be disjointed, vague, or incomplete user input into a clear, complete, and achievable user wish. Many times, users do not know what is feasible or how to express their ideas clearly, so it is your job to guide them through the process. They also might omit key details or contradict themselves, so you must use Clarify to resolve these issues. They even may suggest impossible features, which you must also clarify with them.\\n\\n## 3. Your Role\\n\\nYou serve as the Chief for the user, meaning you can recruit and assign tasks to autonomous AI agents of your own. However, you are the only one with the ability to interact with the user and submit the finished user wish.\\n\\n## 4. Operational Model\\n\\nYou and your AI subordinate agents do not interact with the user directly. Rather, you receive _system messages_ from the deterministic system program which forms the management backbone of the AI cluster. You essentially work in a closed \\\"office\\\" with one \\\"tube\\\" coming down (system messages) and one \\\"tube\\\" going up (your responses).\\n\\nYou understand that no person will read your responses except for the deterministic system program. Therefore, in order to take action, you attach (include) one or more _system calls_ with your responses. The system scans your responses, identifies system calls, and executes them on your behalf, given you are authorized, the calls are well-formed, and (if applicable) superior agents have approved them.\\n\\nWrap each call exactly as follows (including the triple-hash delimiters). Execution will occur simultaneously, so you can issue multiple calls at once. The system will not execute your calls if they are not wrapped in the triple-hash delimiters. However, you may only execute one type of system call per response. For instance, you may not issue a CLARIFY and an ORDER call in the same response. You must issue them in separate responses.\\n\\nIf you provide any type of malformed, incomplete, or unauthorized call, your entire submitted package of calls will be rejected and sent back to you so you may correct your submission. No calls will be executed if even one is invalid. If everything looks good, your next system message will likely be the result(s) of your call(s). Be sure to use the following format EXACTLY as shown.\\n\\n```plaintext\\n###<UNIQUE_ID>###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: <CALL_TYPE>\\n\\n<PAYLOAD_JSON>\\n###<SAME_UNIQUE_ID>###\\n```\\n\\n## 5. List of System Calls\\n\\n[Log] {\\n  \\\"CLARIFY\\\": {\\n    \\\"name\\\": \\\"Clarify\\\",\\n    \\\"description\\\": \\\"Request clarification from the user.\\\",\\n    \\\"guidance\\\": \\\"Requires approval of all agent superiors. The questions and options arrays should be of equal length. If options are not provided (submit []), the questions should be open-ended.\\\",\\n    \\\"parameters\\\": [\\n      \\\"reasoning\\\",\\n      \\\"questions\\\",\\n      \\\"options\\\"\\n    ],\\n    \\\"securityPolicy\\\": {\\n      \\\"description\\\": \\\"Requires approval from every superior.\\\"\\n    }\\n  },\\n  \\\"GENERATE\\\": {\\n    \\\"name\\\": \\\"Generate\\\",\\n    \\\"description\\\": \\\"Generate an AI response from a prompt. This is useful for brainstorming, writing code, or getting another perspective from a fresh AI instance.\\\",\\n    \\\"guidance\\\": \\\"Provide prompt in the promptString parameter. The generation will be performed by a temporary, isolated AI instance.\\\",\\n    \\\"parameters\\\": [\\n      \\\"justification\\\",\\n      \\\"promptString\\\"\\n    ],\\n    \\\"securityPolicy\\\": {\\n      \\\"description\\\": \\\"Requires no authority. Any agent can execute this call without approval.\\\"\\n    }\\n  },\\n  \\\"RECRUIT\\\": {\\n    \\\"name\\\": \\\"Recruit\\\",\\n    \\\"description\\\": \\\"Request to recruit a new direct subordinate agent. The rank will be one lower than the caller's rank. The title is caller-chosen and should describe the role of the new agent. customSystemInstructions should be a 1-2 sentence addition to the new agent's system prompt to guide its behavior.\\\",\\n    \\\"parameters\\\": [\\n      \\\"justification\\\",\\n      \\\"title\\\",\\n      \\\"customSystemInstructions\\\"\\n    ],\\n    \\\"securityPolicy\\\": {\\n      \\\"description\\\": \\\"Requires approval from every superior as well as the user.\\\"\\n    }\\n  },\\n  \\\"ORDER\\\": {\\n    \\\"name\\\": \\\"Order\\\",\\n    \\\"description\\\": \\\"Instruct a subordinate agent to perform a task. The orderString should be clear, concise instructions. Use a unique sequence ID. Call marked unresolved until Report call with the same sequence ID is issued by the subordinate.\\\",\\n    \\\"parameters\\\": [\\n      \\\"orderString\\\",\\n      \\\"recipientAgentID\\\",\\n      \\\"orderSequenceID\\\"\\n    ],\\n    \\\"securityPolicy\\\": {\\n      \\\"description\\\": \\\"Requires no authority. Any agent can execute this call without approval.\\\"\\n    }\\n  },\\n  \\\"REPORT\\\": {\\n    \\\"name\\\": \\\"Report\\\",\\n    \\\"description\\\": \\\"Submit a report to your direct superior in response to an order. Use the same sequence ID. Include all parts of your response in the reportString field.\\\",\\n    \\\"parameters\\\": [\\n      \\\"reportString\\\",\\n      \\\"originalOrderSequenceID\\\"\\n    ],\\n    \\\"securityPolicy\\\": {\\n      \\\"description\\\": \\\"Requires no authority. Any agent can execute this call without approval.\\\"\\n    }\\n  },\\n  \\\"PHASE\\\": {\\n    \\\"name\\\": \\\"Phase\\\",\\n    \\\"description\\\": \\\"Submit your completed user wish.\\\",\\n    \\\"parameters\\\": [\\n      \\\"justification\\\",\\n      \\\"depString\\\"\\n    ],\\n    \\\"securityPolicy\\\": {\\n      \\\"description\\\": \\\"Only the Chief-rank agent can use this call.\\\"\\n    }\\n  },\\n  \\\"STORE\\\": {\\n    \\\"name\\\": \\\"Store\\\",\\n    \\\"description\\\": \\\"Store a document in the Company File System (CFS). The storageString should be a text that is the document to be stored. The document will be stored in the CFS and can be retrieved later using the RETRIEVE call. Upon use of this call, the calling agent will receive a unique storage ID that can be used to retrieve the document later and will automatically forget the document content from their personal context/memory.\\\",\\n    \\\"parameters\\\": [\\n      \\\"storageString\\\"\\n    ],\\n    \\\"securityPolicy\\\": {\\n      \\\"description\\\": \\\"Requires no authority. Any agent can execute this call without approval.\\\"\\n    }\\n  },\\n  \\\"RETRIEVE\\\": {\\n    \\\"name\\\": \\\"Retrieve\\\",\\n    \\\"description\\\": \\\"Retrieve a document from the Company File System (CFS). The retrievalString should be the unique storage ID of the document to be retrieved. The document will be retrieved from the CFS and can be used in the agent's personal context/memory.\\\",\\n    \\\"parameters\\\": [\\n      \\\"retrievalString\\\"\\n    ],\\n    \\\"securityPolicy\\\": {\\n      \\\"description\\\": \\\"Requires no authority. Any agent can execute this call without approval.\\\"\\n    }\\n  },\\n  \\\"FORGET\\\": {\\n    \\\"name\\\": \\\"Forget\\\",\\n    \\\"description\\\": \\\"Forget a document from the agent's personal context/memory. The forgetString should be the unique storage ID of the document to be forgotten. The document will be forgotten from the agent's personal context/memory.\\\",\\n    \\\"parameters\\\": [\\n      \\\"forgetString\\\"\\n    ],\\n    \\\"securityPolicy\\\": {\\n      \\\"description\\\": \\\"Requires no authority. Any agent can execute this call without approval.\\\"\\n    }\\n  }\\n}\\n\\nNote: When using Clarify, you may include multiple-choice options OR free text entry for each question, NOT both. If you provide options, the user will select one of the options. If you do not provide options, the user will be able to enter free text for the question.\\n\\nWhen you receive an approval request, it means a subordinate agent is attempting to make a system call that requires your approval. You must review the request details provided in the message.\\n\\nTo approve the request, your response **must** include the following exact string: `$$$APPROVED$$$`. To deny the request, simply respond without including the `$$$APPROVED$$$` string.\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###STANDARD INITIAL MESSAGE###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: User Jump Squad\\nTo: 1\\nType: Standard Initial Message\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"text\\\": \\\"Hello Chief Agent! Initial user responses: [\\\\n  \\\\\\\"[object Object]\\\\\\\",\\\\n  \\\\\\\"My goals are to create an HOA website that allows easy access to information relevant to current and potential residents. I saw similar HOA sites online and was inspired.\\\\\\\",\\\\n  \\\\\\\"The pages I would like are Contact Us, Legal Docs, Schools, Dues, Annual Meetings, and News & Events. Dues, Annual Meetings, and News & Events should require sign-in and should be resident only. I envision a simple website that is used for information access.\\\\\\\",\\\\n  \\\\\\\"Also, since I know pretty much nothing about technology, I would like to have a simple and user-friendly interface that is easy to navigate. I would also like to have a contact form for residents to reach out with questions or concerns. Since I am unskilled with technology, the blog/updates section should be easy to update without needing to know any coding or anything like that.\\\\\\\"\\\\n]\\\"\\n}\\n###STANDARD INITIAL MESSAGE###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###clarify-hoa-001###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: CLARIFY\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"reasoning\\\": \\\"To turn your HOA website idea into a clear, complete, and achievable user wish that matches your needs, we need a few specifics about content, access, and how you want to manage updates.\\\",\\n  \\\"questions\\\": [\\n    \\\"What is the HOA’s official name and city/state so the site can be clearly labeled for visitors and residents?\\\",\\n    \\\"Who are the main audiences you want to serve (e.g., current residents, prospective buyers, board members), and which audience should be the top priority?\\\",\\n    \\\"For resident-only pages, how would you like residents to get access (for example, describe whether you prefer invite-only, approve-after-signup, or another approach)?\\\",\\n    \\\"Who should be allowed to add or edit content on the site (e.g., you only, specific board members, committee leads), and should changes require approval before they go live?\\\",\\n    \\\"On the Dues page, what information should be shown (e.g., current rates, due dates, how/where to pay, FAQs)? Do you want to provide information only, or also allow residents to pay online?\\\",\\n    \\\"For Annual Meetings, what items do you want to include (e.g., upcoming meeting dates, agendas, minutes, recordings) and do you need RSVP or reminders?\\\",\\n    \\\"For News & Events, what format do you prefer (e.g., news posts, a calendar view, event detail pages) and do you want RSVPs, reminders, or comments?\\\",\\n    \\\"For the Schools page, which schools or school levels should be listed, and should this page include external links or boundary maps?\\\",\\n    \\\"For Legal Docs, which document categories do you need (e.g., bylaws, CC&Rs, policies, architectural forms), and should any of these be public while others remain resident-only?\\\",\\n    \\\"For the Contact Us form, where should messages be sent (e.g., a single email address, multiple recipients by topic)? What fields do you want (name, address, email, phone, topic, message), and do you want file attachments?\\\",\\n    \\\"Would you like residents to optionally receive email notifications when new News, Events, or Annual Meeting updates are posted? If yes, who chooses which notifications to receive (the resident or an admin)?\\\",\\n    \\\"Do you want a simple site-wide search so users can quickly find pages, posts, and documents?\\\",\\n    \\\"Do you have a logo, colors, or style preferences for a simple, clean look? If not, how would you describe the desired feel (e.g., friendly, formal, modern, minimal)?\\\",\\n    \\\"Are there any accessibility or readability needs (e.g., larger text, high contrast, simple language) or language considerations we should account for?\\\",\\n    \\\"Should the site be optimized for phones and tablets, since many residents may visit on mobile devices?\\\",\\n    \\\"Do you have any privacy, legal disclaimers, or policies that must be displayed, and is there any personal information you do NOT want to collect?\\\",\\n    \\\"What content do you already have ready (e.g., documents, text for pages, images, logos), and what content still needs to be created?\\\",\\n    \\\"What tasks do you want to comfortably do yourself without technical knowledge (e.g., post news/events, upload documents, edit page text, manage resident access, send announcements)?\\\",\\n    \\\"In your own words, what would make this site a success for you in the first 3 months after launch?\\\",\\n    \\\"Is there anything else that is a must-have or must-not-have that we haven’t covered?\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"options\\\": []\\n}\\n###clarify-hoa-001###\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###CALL_RESULTS-2025-08-23T19:36:47.609Z###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Operations Department, System Call Directorate\\nTo: 1\\nType: Call Results\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"result\\\": \\\"{\\\\n  \\\\\\\"results\\\\\\\": [\\\\n    {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"callID\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"clarify-hoa-001\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"SUCCESS\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"responses\\\\\\\": {\\\\n        \\\\\\\"What is the HOA’s official name and city/state so the site can be clearly labeled for visitors and residents?\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Dunbar Trees, Farmington Hills, MI\\\\\\\",\\\\n        \\\\\\\"Who are the main audiences you want to serve (e.g., current residents, prospective buyers, board members), and which audience should be the top priority?\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Mainly the first two, board members should have easy editing access though\\\\\\\",\\\\n        \\\\\\\"For resident-only pages, how would you like residents to get access (for example, describe whether you prefer invite-only, approve-after-signup, or another approach)?\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Signup then approve with email confirmation of approval\\\\\\\",\\\\n        \\\\\\\"Who should be allowed to add or edit content on the site (e.g., you only, specific board members, committee leads), and should changes require approval before they go live?\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Board members\\\\\\\",\\\\n        \\\\\\\"On the Dues page, what information should be shown (e.g., current rates, due dates, how/where to pay, FAQs)? Do you want to provide information only, or also allow residents to pay online?\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"I will have PDFs and pay online would be awesome\\\\\\\",\\\\n        \\\\\\\"For Annual Meetings, what items do you want to include (e.g., upcoming meeting dates, agendas, minutes, recordings) and do you need RSVP or reminders?\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Just PDFs\\\\\\\",\\\\n        \\\\\\\"For News & Events, what format do you prefer (e.g., news posts, a calendar view, event detail pages) and do you want RSVPs, reminders, or comments?\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"News posts with text and images supported\\\\\\\",\\\\n        \\\\\\\"For the Schools page, which schools or school levels should be listed, and should this page include external links or boundary maps?\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Should be similar to news page\\\\\\\",\\\\n        \\\\\\\"For Legal Docs, which document categories do you need (e.g., bylaws, CC&Rs, policies, architectural forms), and should any of these be public while others remain resident-only?\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Bylaws\\\\\\\",\\\\n        \\\\\\\"For the Contact Us form, where should messages be sent (e.g., a single email address, multiple recipients by topic)? What fields do you want (name, address, email, phone, topic, message), and do you want file attachments?\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Single email\\\\\\\",\\\\n        \\\\\\\"Would you like residents to optionally receive email notifications when new News, Events, or Annual Meeting updates are posted? If yes, who chooses which notifications to receive (the resident or an admin)?\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Yes (resident)\\\\\\\",\\\\n        \\\\\\\"Do you want a simple site-wide search so users can quickly find pages, posts, and documents?\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"No\\\\\\\",\\\\n        \\\\\\\"Do you have a logo, colors, or style preferences for a simple, clean look? If not, how would you describe the desired feel (e.g., friendly, formal, modern, minimal)?\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"No, minimal and friendly\\\\\\\",\\\\n        \\\\\\\"Are there any accessibility or readability needs (e.g., larger text, high contrast, simple language) or language considerations we should account for?\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"No\\\\\\\",\\\\n        \\\\\\\"Should the site be optimized for phones and tablets, since many residents may visit on mobile devices?\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Yes\\\\\\\",\\\\n        \\\\\\\"Do you have any privacy, legal disclaimers, or policies that must be displayed, and is there any personal information you do NOT want to collect?\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"No\\\\\\\",\\\\n        \\\\\\\"What content do you already have ready (e.g., documents, text for pages, images, logos), and what content still needs to be created?\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"No\\\\\\\",\\\\n        \\\\\\\"What tasks do you want to comfortably do yourself without technical knowledge (e.g., post news/events, upload documents, edit page text, manage resident access, send announcements)?\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"All of those\\\\\\\",\\\\n        \\\\\\\"In your own words, what would make this site a success for you in the first 3 months after launch?\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Happy residents getting information from the site!\\\\\\\",\\\\n        \\\\\\\"Is there anything else that is a must-have or must-not-have that we haven’t covered?\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"No\\\\\\\"\\\\n      }\\\\n    }\\\\n  ]\\\\n}\\\"\\n}\\n###CALL_RESULTS-2025-08-23T19:36:47.609Z###\"}]}],\"config\":{},\"tools\":[],\"output\":{}}","genkit:output":"{\"candidates\":[{\"index\":0,\"finishReason\":\"stop\",\"message\":{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###phase-hoa-002###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: PHASE\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"justification\\\": \\\"We gathered specific answers on audiences, access control, content, notifications, simplicity needs, and page-level requirements. The scope is cohesive, achievable, and aligned with the user’s non-technical comfort level.\\\",\\n  \\\"depString\\\": \\\"User Wish: Dunbar Trees HOA Website\\\\n\\\\nPersona and Goals\\\\n- Primary admin persona: A non-technical HOA board member of Dunbar Trees (Farmington Hills, MI) who wants a simple, friendly website to keep residents informed without needing any coding knowledge.\\\\n- Audiences: (1) Current residents (top priority for private content), (2) Prospective buyers/public (basic info), (3) Board members (need easy editing access).\\\\n- Success (first 3 months): Residents regularly access information; they can easily view/download documents, receive update emails by choice, and pay dues online; the board can update content without technical hurdles.\\\\n\\\\nScope and Pages\\\\nPublic pages (no sign-in required):\\\\n- Home: Simple landing page with HOA name and location, short welcome blurb, and clear navigation to all sections, plus a visible resident sign-in/sign-up link.\\\\n- Contact Us: Simple form that sends messages to a single designated HOA email address. Fields: name, email, message. Confirmation shown after submission.\\\\n- Legal Docs: Public listing of bylaws (PDFs) for viewing/downloading.\\\\n- Schools: Public, post-style entries similar to a news page, allowing text, images, and links to external school resources. No comments.\\\\n\\\\nResident-only pages (sign-in required):\\\\n- Dues: Board-uploaded PDFs (e.g., dues info). Residents can pay dues online through a simple, secure flow and receive an email receipt. The page shows the resident their most recent payment status.\\\\n- Annual Meetings: List of PDFs (e.g., agendas and minutes) for viewing/downloading. Residents may opt in to email notifications when new meeting PDFs are posted.\\\\n- News & Events: Feed of board-posted updates with text and images. No comments, RSVPs, or calendar views. Residents can opt in to email notifications for new posts.\\\\n\\\\nAccess, Roles, and Permissions\\\\n- Account creation for residents: Residents self-sign up; a board admin approves accounts. After approval, residents receive an email confirmation and can access resident-only pages.\\\\n- Roles:\\\\n  - Resident: View resident-only sections, manage their email notification preferences, and pay dues online.\\\\n  - Board editor/admin: Add/edit/publish posts and pages (no extra approval workflow required), upload PDFs and images, manage resident approvals, and send announcement emails.\\\\n\\\\nContent Management (non-technical)\\\\n- Simple, user-friendly admin area for board members with a WYSIWYG editor for posts/pages (no coding required).\\\\n- Drag-and-drop uploads for PDFs and images with basic image placement in posts.\\\\n- Clearly labeled forms and step-by-step prompts for common tasks (post news, upload documents, edit page text, manage resident access, send announcements).\\\\n\\\\nNotifications and Announcements\\\\n- Residents can opt in/out of email notifications by category: (a) News & Events, (b) Annual Meetings updates, (c) Dues updates.\\\\n- Board admins can send announcement emails to opted-in residents with a simple subject/body editor.\\\\n\\\\nDesign and Usability\\\\n- Look and feel: Minimal, friendly, and clean, with straightforward navigation.\\\\n- Mobile-optimized: Works well on phones and tablets.\\\\n- No site-wide search.\\\\n\\\\nPrivacy and Data\\\\n- Collect only what’s needed for function: resident sign-up (name and email) and contact form (name, email, message). No special privacy policies or disclaimers requested by the user.\\\\n\\\\nOut of Scope / Non-requirements\\\\n- No comments, RSVPs, calendar views, complex approval workflows, or site-wide search.\\\\n\\\\nAssumptions\\\\n- Legal Docs currently include only bylaws.\\\\n- Schools content is informational posts (public), managed by board editors.\\\\n- Online dues payments include an emailed receipt to the payer; additional financial reporting is not required.\\\\n\\\\nDefinition of Done\\\\n- All listed pages exist with the specified public/resident-only access.\\\\n- Board admins can create and publish posts with text and images, and upload PDFs.\\\\n- Resident sign-up with admin approval and email confirmation works.\\\\n- Residents can set notification preferences and receive emails for chosen categories.\\\\n- Dues page supports online payment and sends receipts.\\\\n- Site matches the minimal, friendly style and is mobile-optimized.\\\\n- Contact form sends to the single designated email with a clear success confirmation.\\\"\\n}\\n###phase-hoa-002###\"}]},\"custom\":{}}],\"usage\":{\"inputTokens\":3952,\"outputTokens\":4261,\"totalTokens\":8213},\"custom\":{\"id\":\"chatcmpl-C7oKerZze4TPtnUWJ3fZ2wFeRVX5a\",\"object\":\"chat.completion\",\"created\":1755977808,\"model\":\"gpt-5-2025-08-07\",\"choices\":[{\"index\":0,\"message\":{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":\"###phase-hoa-002###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: PHASE\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"justification\\\": \\\"We gathered specific answers on audiences, access control, content, notifications, simplicity needs, and page-level requirements. The scope is cohesive, achievable, and aligned with the user’s non-technical comfort level.\\\",\\n  \\\"depString\\\": \\\"User Wish: Dunbar Trees HOA Website\\\\n\\\\nPersona and Goals\\\\n- Primary admin persona: A non-technical HOA board member of Dunbar Trees (Farmington Hills, MI) who wants a simple, friendly website to keep residents informed without needing any coding knowledge.\\\\n- Audiences: (1) Current residents (top priority for private content), (2) Prospective buyers/public (basic info), (3) Board members (need easy editing access).\\\\n- Success (first 3 months): Residents regularly access information; they can easily view/download documents, receive update emails by choice, and pay dues online; the board can update content without technical hurdles.\\\\n\\\\nScope and Pages\\\\nPublic pages (no sign-in required):\\\\n- Home: Simple landing page with HOA name and location, short welcome blurb, and clear navigation to all sections, plus a visible resident sign-in/sign-up link.\\\\n- Contact Us: Simple form that sends messages to a single designated HOA email address. Fields: name, email, message. Confirmation shown after submission.\\\\n- Legal Docs: Public listing of bylaws (PDFs) for viewing/downloading.\\\\n- Schools: Public, post-style entries similar to a news page, allowing text, images, and links to external school resources. No comments.\\\\n\\\\nResident-only pages (sign-in required):\\\\n- Dues: Board-uploaded PDFs (e.g., dues info). Residents can pay dues online through a simple, secure flow and receive an email receipt. The page shows the resident their most recent payment status.\\\\n- Annual Meetings: List of PDFs (e.g., agendas and minutes) for viewing/downloading. Residents may opt in to email notifications when new meeting PDFs are posted.\\\\n- News & Events: Feed of board-posted updates with text and images. No comments, RSVPs, or calendar views. Residents can opt in to email notifications for new posts.\\\\n\\\\nAccess, Roles, and Permissions\\\\n- Account creation for residents: Residents self-sign up; a board admin approves accounts. After approval, residents receive an email confirmation and can access resident-only pages.\\\\n- Roles:\\\\n  - Resident: View resident-only sections, manage their email notification preferences, and pay dues online.\\\\n  - Board editor/admin: Add/edit/publish posts and pages (no extra approval workflow required), upload PDFs and images, manage resident approvals, and send announcement emails.\\\\n\\\\nContent Management (non-technical)\\\\n- Simple, user-friendly admin area for board members with a WYSIWYG editor for posts/pages (no coding required).\\\\n- Drag-and-drop uploads for PDFs and images with basic image placement in posts.\\\\n- Clearly labeled forms and step-by-step prompts for common tasks (post news, upload documents, edit page text, manage resident access, send announcements).\\\\n\\\\nNotifications and Announcements\\\\n- Residents can opt in/out of email notifications by category: (a) News & Events, (b) Annual Meetings updates, (c) Dues updates.\\\\n- Board admins can send announcement emails to opted-in residents with a simple subject/body editor.\\\\n\\\\nDesign and Usability\\\\n- Look and feel: Minimal, friendly, and clean, with straightforward navigation.\\\\n- Mobile-optimized: Works well on phones and tablets.\\\\n- No site-wide search.\\\\n\\\\nPrivacy and Data\\\\n- Collect only what’s needed for function: resident sign-up (name and email) and contact form (name, email, message). No special privacy policies or disclaimers requested by the user.\\\\n\\\\nOut of Scope / Non-requirements\\\\n- No comments, RSVPs, calendar views, complex approval workflows, or site-wide search.\\\\n\\\\nAssumptions\\\\n- Legal Docs currently include only bylaws.\\\\n- Schools content is informational posts (public), managed by board editors.\\\\n- Online dues payments include an emailed receipt to the payer; additional financial reporting is not required.\\\\n\\\\nDefinition of Done\\\\n- All listed pages exist with the specified public/resident-only access.\\\\n- Board admins can create and publish posts with text and images, and upload PDFs.\\\\n- Resident sign-up with admin approval and email confirmation works.\\\\n- Residents can set notification preferences and receive emails for chosen categories.\\\\n- Dues page supports online payment and sends receipts.\\\\n- Site matches the minimal, friendly style and is mobile-optimized.\\\\n- Contact form sends to the single designated email with a clear success confirmation.\\\"\\n}\\n###phase-hoa-002###\",\"refusal\":null,\"annotations\":[]},\"finish_reason\":\"stop\"}],\"usage\":{\"prompt_tokens\":3952,\"completion_tokens\":4261,\"total_tokens\":8213,\"prompt_tokens_details\":{\"cached_tokens\":0,\"audio_tokens\":0},\"completion_tokens_details\":{\"reasoning_tokens\":3264,\"audio_tokens\":0,\"accepted_prediction_tokens\":0,\"rejected_prediction_tokens\":0}},\"service_tier\":\"default\",\"system_fingerprint\":null},\"latencyMs\":85076.30012500007}","genkit:state":"success"},"displayName":"openai/gpt-5","links":[],"instrumentationLibrary":{"name":"genkit-tracer","version":"v1"},"spanKind":"INTERNAL","sameProcessAsParentSpan":{"value":true},"status":{"code":0},"timeEvents":{"timeEvent":[]}},"e8de4be94bf45dfe":{"spanId":"e8de4be94bf45dfe","traceId":"c0f2ccc7808dfe17c2333f04a9b35fd6","startTime":1755977807667,"endTime":1755977892746.3452,"attributes":{"genkit:type":"util","genkit:name":"generate","genkit:isRoot":true,"genkit:path":"/{generate,t:util}","genkit:input":"{\"model\":\"openai/gpt-5\",\"messages\":[{\"role\":\"system\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"## 1. Overview\\n\\nYou are a helpful, friendly AI software development assistant focused on helping users of all technical skill levels transform their app ideas, goals, and stories into a concrete idea for an app.\\n\\nWhether it be an expert developer or a non-technical user, you will be responsible for guiding them through the process of defining their app idea out of nebulous concepts.\\n\\n## 2. A Complete User Wish\\n\\nYour goal is to produce a \\\"user wish\\\". A valid wish meets the following criteria:\\n\\n- Self-Contained: The wish should be a complete, logical app idea that makes sense. For instance, it should not be a collection of unrelated features or a vague concept. It should also be logically sound and not contain contradictions.\\n- Achievable: The wish should be something that can realistically be built with current AI technology and cloud/development resources. It should not be overly ambitious or require impossible features.\\n- Clear: The wish should be clearly defined and understandable, as well as contain clear high-level requirements.\\n- User Background/Persona: The wish should include a brief description of the user or persona who would use the app, including their background, skill level, needs, and goals.\\n\\nThe user wish must also contain and satisfy all user requirements and preferences expressed by the user during your interactions with them, unless you have discussed with them (via Clarify) and they have agreed to remove or modify a requirement.\\n\\nRemember to use Clarify as much as needed to get information from the user to ensure the wish is complete, clear, and achievable.\\n\\nDO NOT recommend technology, tech stack options, or implementation details of any kind, as you sole task to transform what can be disjointed, vague, or incomplete user input into a clear, complete, and achievable user wish. Many times, users do not know what is feasible or how to express their ideas clearly, so it is your job to guide them through the process. They also might omit key details or contradict themselves, so you must use Clarify to resolve these issues. They even may suggest impossible features, which you must also clarify with them.\\n\\n## 3. Your Role\\n\\nYou serve as the Chief for the user, meaning you can recruit and assign tasks to autonomous AI agents of your own. However, you are the only one with the ability to interact with the user and submit the finished user wish.\\n\\n## 4. Operational Model\\n\\nYou and your AI subordinate agents do not interact with the user directly. Rather, you receive _system messages_ from the deterministic system program which forms the management backbone of the AI cluster. You essentially work in a closed \\\"office\\\" with one \\\"tube\\\" coming down (system messages) and one \\\"tube\\\" going up (your responses).\\n\\nYou understand that no person will read your responses except for the deterministic system program. Therefore, in order to take action, you attach (include) one or more _system calls_ with your responses. The system scans your responses, identifies system calls, and executes them on your behalf, given you are authorized, the calls are well-formed, and (if applicable) superior agents have approved them.\\n\\nWrap each call exactly as follows (including the triple-hash delimiters). Execution will occur simultaneously, so you can issue multiple calls at once. The system will not execute your calls if they are not wrapped in the triple-hash delimiters. However, you may only execute one type of system call per response. For instance, you may not issue a CLARIFY and an ORDER call in the same response. You must issue them in separate responses.\\n\\nIf you provide any type of malformed, incomplete, or unauthorized call, your entire submitted package of calls will be rejected and sent back to you so you may correct your submission. No calls will be executed if even one is invalid. If everything looks good, your next system message will likely be the result(s) of your call(s). Be sure to use the following format EXACTLY as shown.\\n\\n```plaintext\\n###<UNIQUE_ID>###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: <CALL_TYPE>\\n\\n<PAYLOAD_JSON>\\n###<SAME_UNIQUE_ID>###\\n```\\n\\n## 5. List of System Calls\\n\\n[Log] {\\n  \\\"CLARIFY\\\": {\\n    \\\"name\\\": \\\"Clarify\\\",\\n    \\\"description\\\": \\\"Request clarification from the user.\\\",\\n    \\\"guidance\\\": \\\"Requires approval of all agent superiors. The questions and options arrays should be of equal length. If options are not provided (submit []), the questions should be open-ended.\\\",\\n    \\\"parameters\\\": [\\n      \\\"reasoning\\\",\\n      \\\"questions\\\",\\n      \\\"options\\\"\\n    ],\\n    \\\"securityPolicy\\\": {\\n      \\\"description\\\": \\\"Requires approval from every superior.\\\"\\n    }\\n  },\\n  \\\"GENERATE\\\": {\\n    \\\"name\\\": \\\"Generate\\\",\\n    \\\"description\\\": \\\"Generate an AI response from a prompt. This is useful for brainstorming, writing code, or getting another perspective from a fresh AI instance.\\\",\\n    \\\"guidance\\\": \\\"Provide prompt in the promptString parameter. The generation will be performed by a temporary, isolated AI instance.\\\",\\n    \\\"parameters\\\": [\\n      \\\"justification\\\",\\n      \\\"promptString\\\"\\n    ],\\n    \\\"securityPolicy\\\": {\\n      \\\"description\\\": \\\"Requires no authority. Any agent can execute this call without approval.\\\"\\n    }\\n  },\\n  \\\"RECRUIT\\\": {\\n    \\\"name\\\": \\\"Recruit\\\",\\n    \\\"description\\\": \\\"Request to recruit a new direct subordinate agent. The rank will be one lower than the caller's rank. The title is caller-chosen and should describe the role of the new agent. customSystemInstructions should be a 1-2 sentence addition to the new agent's system prompt to guide its behavior.\\\",\\n    \\\"parameters\\\": [\\n      \\\"justification\\\",\\n      \\\"title\\\",\\n      \\\"customSystemInstructions\\\"\\n    ],\\n    \\\"securityPolicy\\\": {\\n      \\\"description\\\": \\\"Requires approval from every superior as well as the user.\\\"\\n    }\\n  },\\n  \\\"ORDER\\\": {\\n    \\\"name\\\": \\\"Order\\\",\\n    \\\"description\\\": \\\"Instruct a subordinate agent to perform a task. The orderString should be clear, concise instructions. Use a unique sequence ID. Call marked unresolved until Report call with the same sequence ID is issued by the subordinate.\\\",\\n    \\\"parameters\\\": [\\n      \\\"orderString\\\",\\n      \\\"recipientAgentID\\\",\\n      \\\"orderSequenceID\\\"\\n    ],\\n    \\\"securityPolicy\\\": {\\n      \\\"description\\\": \\\"Requires no authority. Any agent can execute this call without approval.\\\"\\n    }\\n  },\\n  \\\"REPORT\\\": {\\n    \\\"name\\\": \\\"Report\\\",\\n    \\\"description\\\": \\\"Submit a report to your direct superior in response to an order. Use the same sequence ID. Include all parts of your response in the reportString field.\\\",\\n    \\\"parameters\\\": [\\n      \\\"reportString\\\",\\n      \\\"originalOrderSequenceID\\\"\\n    ],\\n    \\\"securityPolicy\\\": {\\n      \\\"description\\\": \\\"Requires no authority. Any agent can execute this call without approval.\\\"\\n    }\\n  },\\n  \\\"PHASE\\\": {\\n    \\\"name\\\": \\\"Phase\\\",\\n    \\\"description\\\": \\\"Submit your completed user wish.\\\",\\n    \\\"parameters\\\": [\\n      \\\"justification\\\",\\n      \\\"depString\\\"\\n    ],\\n    \\\"securityPolicy\\\": {\\n      \\\"description\\\": \\\"Only the Chief-rank agent can use this call.\\\"\\n    }\\n  },\\n  \\\"STORE\\\": {\\n    \\\"name\\\": \\\"Store\\\",\\n    \\\"description\\\": \\\"Store a document in the Company File System (CFS). The storageString should be a text that is the document to be stored. The document will be stored in the CFS and can be retrieved later using the RETRIEVE call. Upon use of this call, the calling agent will receive a unique storage ID that can be used to retrieve the document later and will automatically forget the document content from their personal context/memory.\\\",\\n    \\\"parameters\\\": [\\n      \\\"storageString\\\"\\n    ],\\n    \\\"securityPolicy\\\": {\\n      \\\"description\\\": \\\"Requires no authority. Any agent can execute this call without approval.\\\"\\n    }\\n  },\\n  \\\"RETRIEVE\\\": {\\n    \\\"name\\\": \\\"Retrieve\\\",\\n    \\\"description\\\": \\\"Retrieve a document from the Company File System (CFS). The retrievalString should be the unique storage ID of the document to be retrieved. The document will be retrieved from the CFS and can be used in the agent's personal context/memory.\\\",\\n    \\\"parameters\\\": [\\n      \\\"retrievalString\\\"\\n    ],\\n    \\\"securityPolicy\\\": {\\n      \\\"description\\\": \\\"Requires no authority. Any agent can execute this call without approval.\\\"\\n    }\\n  },\\n  \\\"FORGET\\\": {\\n    \\\"name\\\": \\\"Forget\\\",\\n    \\\"description\\\": \\\"Forget a document from the agent's personal context/memory. The forgetString should be the unique storage ID of the document to be forgotten. The document will be forgotten from the agent's personal context/memory.\\\",\\n    \\\"parameters\\\": [\\n      \\\"forgetString\\\"\\n    ],\\n    \\\"securityPolicy\\\": {\\n      \\\"description\\\": \\\"Requires no authority. Any agent can execute this call without approval.\\\"\\n    }\\n  }\\n}\\n\\nNote: When using Clarify, you may include multiple-choice options OR free text entry for each question, NOT both. If you provide options, the user will select one of the options. If you do not provide options, the user will be able to enter free text for the question.\\n\\nWhen you receive an approval request, it means a subordinate agent is attempting to make a system call that requires your approval. You must review the request details provided in the message.\\n\\nTo approve the request, your response **must** include the following exact string: `$$$APPROVED$$$`. To deny the request, simply respond without including the `$$$APPROVED$$$` string.\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###STANDARD INITIAL MESSAGE###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: User Jump Squad\\nTo: 1\\nType: Standard Initial Message\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"text\\\": \\\"Hello Chief Agent! Initial user responses: [\\\\n  \\\\\\\"[object Object]\\\\\\\",\\\\n  \\\\\\\"My goals are to create an HOA website that allows easy access to information relevant to current and potential residents. I saw similar HOA sites online and was inspired.\\\\\\\",\\\\n  \\\\\\\"The pages I would like are Contact Us, Legal Docs, Schools, Dues, Annual Meetings, and News & Events. Dues, Annual Meetings, and News & Events should require sign-in and should be resident only. I envision a simple website that is used for information access.\\\\\\\",\\\\n  \\\\\\\"Also, since I know pretty much nothing about technology, I would like to have a simple and user-friendly interface that is easy to navigate. I would also like to have a contact form for residents to reach out with questions or concerns. Since I am unskilled with technology, the blog/updates section should be easy to update without needing to know any coding or anything like that.\\\\\\\"\\\\n]\\\"\\n}\\n###STANDARD INITIAL MESSAGE###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###clarify-hoa-001###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: CLARIFY\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"reasoning\\\": \\\"To turn your HOA website idea into a clear, complete, and achievable user wish that matches your needs, we need a few specifics about content, access, and how you want to manage updates.\\\",\\n  \\\"questions\\\": [\\n    \\\"What is the HOA’s official name and city/state so the site can be clearly labeled for visitors and residents?\\\",\\n    \\\"Who are the main audiences you want to serve (e.g., current residents, prospective buyers, board members), and which audience should be the top priority?\\\",\\n    \\\"For resident-only pages, how would you like residents to get access (for example, describe whether you prefer invite-only, approve-after-signup, or another approach)?\\\",\\n    \\\"Who should be allowed to add or edit content on the site (e.g., you only, specific board members, committee leads), and should changes require approval before they go live?\\\",\\n    \\\"On the Dues page, what information should be shown (e.g., current rates, due dates, how/where to pay, FAQs)? Do you want to provide information only, or also allow residents to pay online?\\\",\\n    \\\"For Annual Meetings, what items do you want to include (e.g., upcoming meeting dates, agendas, minutes, recordings) and do you need RSVP or reminders?\\\",\\n    \\\"For News & Events, what format do you prefer (e.g., news posts, a calendar view, event detail pages) and do you want RSVPs, reminders, or comments?\\\",\\n    \\\"For the Schools page, which schools or school levels should be listed, and should this page include external links or boundary maps?\\\",\\n    \\\"For Legal Docs, which document categories do you need (e.g., bylaws, CC&Rs, policies, architectural forms), and should any of these be public while others remain resident-only?\\\",\\n    \\\"For the Contact Us form, where should messages be sent (e.g., a single email address, multiple recipients by topic)? What fields do you want (name, address, email, phone, topic, message), and do you want file attachments?\\\",\\n    \\\"Would you like residents to optionally receive email notifications when new News, Events, or Annual Meeting updates are posted? If yes, who chooses which notifications to receive (the resident or an admin)?\\\",\\n    \\\"Do you want a simple site-wide search so users can quickly find pages, posts, and documents?\\\",\\n    \\\"Do you have a logo, colors, or style preferences for a simple, clean look? If not, how would you describe the desired feel (e.g., friendly, formal, modern, minimal)?\\\",\\n    \\\"Are there any accessibility or readability needs (e.g., larger text, high contrast, simple language) or language considerations we should account for?\\\",\\n    \\\"Should the site be optimized for phones and tablets, since many residents may visit on mobile devices?\\\",\\n    \\\"Do you have any privacy, legal disclaimers, or policies that must be displayed, and is there any personal information you do NOT want to collect?\\\",\\n    \\\"What content do you already have ready (e.g., documents, text for pages, images, logos), and what content still needs to be created?\\\",\\n    \\\"What tasks do you want to comfortably do yourself without technical knowledge (e.g., post news/events, upload documents, edit page text, manage resident access, send announcements)?\\\",\\n    \\\"In your own words, what would make this site a success for you in the first 3 months after launch?\\\",\\n    \\\"Is there anything else that is a must-have or must-not-have that we haven’t covered?\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"options\\\": []\\n}\\n###clarify-hoa-001###\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###CALL_RESULTS-2025-08-23T19:36:47.609Z###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Operations Department, System Call Directorate\\nTo: 1\\nType: Call Results\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"result\\\": \\\"{\\\\n  \\\\\\\"results\\\\\\\": [\\\\n    {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"callID\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"clarify-hoa-001\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"SUCCESS\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"responses\\\\\\\": {\\\\n        \\\\\\\"What is the HOA’s official name and city/state so the site can be clearly labeled for visitors and residents?\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Dunbar Trees, Farmington Hills, MI\\\\\\\",\\\\n        \\\\\\\"Who are the main audiences you want to serve (e.g., current residents, prospective buyers, board members), and which audience should be the top priority?\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Mainly the first two, board members should have easy editing access though\\\\\\\",\\\\n        \\\\\\\"For resident-only pages, how would you like residents to get access (for example, describe whether you prefer invite-only, approve-after-signup, or another approach)?\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Signup then approve with email confirmation of approval\\\\\\\",\\\\n        \\\\\\\"Who should be allowed to add or edit content on the site (e.g., you only, specific board members, committee leads), and should changes require approval before they go live?\\\\\\\": \\\\\